/*
 =====================================================================
  ESP32 Wi-Fi Manager  (crash-diagnostic revision)

  LED:  VIOLET = AP mode ready (no client) / checking saved Wi-Fi
        BLUE   = phone connected to ESP32 AP
        GREEN  = Wi-Fi connected to router
        RED    = Wi-Fi credentials entered on web page FAILED

  Flow:
   1. Boot: start AP immediately and check saved Wi-Fi at the same time.
   2. AP window is 1 minute from boot; a 10-second button hold opens it
      again for 1 minute.
   3. Serial Monitor updates one live line with the previous-network name,
      30-second search countdown, and 4m30s retry-wait countdown.
   4. If saved Wi-Fi is unavailable, retry every 5 minutes; each attempt
      lasts up to 30 seconds. The AP window closes after 60 seconds; hold
      the button for 10 seconds to open it again.
   4. Captive portal: phone connects to AP -> page opens automatically.
   5. Time sync WITHOUT NTP: HTTP "Date" header (port 80) from
      google.com / cloudflare.com / microsoft.com.
 =====================================================================
*/

